530	
531	If files are not being saved or shared, start with:
532	
533	```sh
534	mise doctor
535	mise dot status
536	```
537	
538	`doctor` summarizes a watcher that is declared but stopped, repeated save
539	failures, an unusable history store, and files being saved less often because
540	they change constantly. It includes the command to start a stopped watcher.
541	
542	`status` gives more detail: whether the watcher is running, declared but
543	stopped, or not declared; the latest save and full scan; the last failure;
544	and each busy file's save interval, last save, and pending edits.
545	
546	These commands read the watcher's saved health report without starting
547	synchronization or changing files. The report lives in `health.json` in the
548	history store. Old reports are marked stale after a few full-scan intervals.
549	A busy file's longer save interval is informational.
550	
551	The watcher sends desktop notifications when a sharing conflict needs
552	attention. See [conflict notifications](#conflict-notifications) for setup
553	and platform support.
