555	## What a checkpoint records
556	
557	History lives in a bare Git repository at `$MISE_STATE_DIR/history/repo.git`,
558	separate from the files you edit. Each checkpoint contains the tracked files
559	and metadata for their paths, tracking settings, variants, encryption, and
560	permissions. The files are ordinary Git tree entries.
561	
562	A symlink is saved as a link. A nested Git repository is saved as a pointer
563	to its commit. mise reports oversized files, special files, and unreadable
564	paths it cannot save. It keeps their previous saved versions while saving
565	other files, so check reported omissions before relying on a checkpoint.
